"""City altitude map for prayer-time correction.

Generated from the Salati 2.0.2 reference database (``cities.altitude``),
GeoNames ``cities500`` (SRTM ``dem`` preferred over ``elevation``), and SRTM
90 m elevations from OpenTopoData for places absent from both.  The map is
keyed by ``"<country>|<normalized city>"`` and decoded lazily on first use.

Values are metres above sea level and may be negative for below-sea-level
cities.  The prayer engine only applies the reference altitude correction
when the value is greater than zero, so negative values are inert.

Matching prefers the reference row with the same normalized city name
(within 50 km); ties and duplicates fall back to the closest coordinate
match, then to a fuzzy name match within 15 km.  GeoNames fills the gaps
left by the reference, and SRTM fills the remaining small localities.
"""

